  "deactivated_at": "2026-09-03T16:11:33.629113+00:00",
  "detailed_description": "The scheme &quot;Pradhan Mantri Matasya Sampada Yojana: Construction of New Grow out Ponds&quot; by the Ministry Of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry &amp; Dairying, Government of India, aims to expand fisheries in various urban and semi-urban areas through the construction of new grow-out ponds. Through this scheme, subsidies are provided for the construction of new grow-out ponds to beneficiaries who are engaged in fisheries.\n<br>\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n1. The applicant must have a Parivar Pehchan Patra (PPP).\n1. The construction of new grow-out ponds subsidy will be provided by the State Government for the expansion of fisheries in various urban/semi-urban areas only under the construction of new grow-out ponds under the Pradhan Mantri Matasya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) scheme.\n1. Central financial assistance for the construction of new grow-out ponds will be provided only for the ponds prepared for fisheries.\n1. The applicant should have own land with clear title or having land on a long-term registered lease, not less than a minimum of 7 years.\n\n",
  "exclusions": null,
